  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Karthikeyan vs The District Collector on 18 March, 2015",
    "facts": "The petitioner is a dealer in food grains and is aggrieved by the seizure of the food grains, by a team led by the District Supply Officer, Thiruvananthapuram, the 2nd respondent, as per Ext.P7 mahazar. The rice stored at the petitioner's premises in plastic bags and intended to be sold in the brand name of 'Nirapara' was seized, on the suspicion that they are food grains intended for supply in the Public Distribution System (PDS). The quantity as specified in the mahazar, was taken possession of. The food grains seized is said to be kept in W.P.(C) No.17347 of 2015 - P the premises of the 5th respondent. The Food Corporation of India (FCI) was directed to make an inspection of the seized articles and file a report. Earlier also the petitioners godown was inspected and goods seized which were subsequently released by the District Collector as per Ext.P10 orders.",
